          "text": "## Modules: CommonJS modules#\n",
          "start_line": 137,
          "end_line": 137
        },
        {
          "id": "line-247",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Loading ECMAScript modules using require()#\n",
          "parent_id": "line-137",
          "start_line": 247,
          "end_line": 247
        },
        {
          "id": "line-251",
          "kind": "table",
          "text": "| Version | Changes |\n| v22.13.0 | This feature no longer emits an experimental warning by default, though the warning can still be emitted by --trace-require-module. |\n| v23.0.0, v22.12.0 | This feature is no longer behind the --experimental-require-module CLI flag. |\n| v22.12.0 | Support 'module.exports' interop export in require(esm). |\n| v22.0.0 | Added in: v22.0.0 |\n",
          "parent_id": "line-247",
          "start_line": 251,
          "end_line": 255
        },
        {
          "id": "line-316",
          "kind": "code",
          "text": "```\nconst Point = require('./point.mjs');\nconsole.log(Point); // [class Point]\n\n// Named exports are lost when 'module.exports' is used\nconst { distance } = require('./point.mjs');\nconsole.log(distance); // undefined copy\n```\n",
          "parent_id": "line-247",
          "start_line": 316,
          "end_line": 323
        },
        {
          "id": "line-338",
          "kind": "code",
          "text": "```\nconst Point = require('./point.mjs');\nconsole.log(Point); // [class Point]\n\nconst { distance } = require('./point.mjs');\nconsole.log(distance); // [Function: distance] copy\n```\n",
          "parent_id": "line-247",
          "start_line": 338,
          "end_line": 344
        },
        {
          "id": "line-350",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Support for loading ES modules using require() is currently experimental and can be disabled using --no-experimental-require-module. To print where this feature is used, use --trace-require-module.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-247",
          "start_line": 350,
          "end_line": 350
        },
        {
          "id": "line-678",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### The module scope#\n",
          "parent_id": "line-137",
          "start_line": 678,
          "end_line": 678
        },
        {
          "id": "line-744",
